  "conclusions": {
    "dominantMeasuredComponent": "Worker raw-build: PDFium calls plus Dart string/rectangle construction; the observations do not separate native extraction from this Dart construction.",
    "normalization": "Hebrew normalization accounts for about one tenth of the instrumented caller interval. Two reference pages have unchanged text/geometry when both Hebrew flags are off; this does not establish that normalization is redundant for other pages or encodings.",
    "residual": "Queue/dispatch/arena/return plus instrumentation bookkeeping remain combined in the outside-worker residual. It is not an isolated transfer measurement or a concurrent-queue measurement.",
    "overhead": "The uninstrumented controls and instrumented callers are close in these ABBA observations. A small or negative observed difference is not evidence of product acceleration or exact zero observer overhead.",
    "productAction": "Prioritize avoiding repeated raw extraction or optimizing the upstream raw-text construction contract. The existing app LRU thrash evidence remains relevant; these source-instrumented diagnostics are not an app optimization.",
    "reference": "UXLC page 1 contains inferred internal spaces, e.g. אֱ לֹהִ֑ ים, before Hebrew normalization as well as after it. Literal and marks-tolerant אלהים both have zero hits in PDFium and the two Poppler layouts. This does not prove how space characters were encoded in PDF objects."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Worker raw-build includes PDFium calls and Dart text/rectangle construction.",
    "The outside-worker residual includes queue, dispatch, arena management, return and instrumentation bookkeeping; it is not isolated transfer time.",
    "Worker counters are read/reset through a separate job outside each timed page interval.",
    "Serial page calls do not measure a concurrent render/search backlog.",
    "Instrumented durations include observer overhead and are not a product speedup.",
    "No native-allocation, Dart-allocation, UI-latency or cold OS-cache claim.",
    "Two independent processes per variant; repeated passes are not independent processes.",
    "Hashes are computed between timed loads and can affect later GC or caches in both variants.",
